cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Pain as Information"
message: >-
  If you use the evidence base, the gate prompts or the harness, please cite
  this repository. If you use a finding, cite the primary source it came from:
  every identifier in evidence/ resolves, and the point of that is that you
  should not have to take this repository's word for anything.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: David
    family-names: Vanheeswijck
    email: david@vanheeswijck.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/davidvanheeswijck/pain-as-information"
abstract: >-
  A research programme on whether chronic neuropathic pain can be treated as a
  signalling problem rather than a tissue problem: read what the nerve is
  actually sending and rewrite it, instead of silencing the nerve by drug,
  current or knife. Contains an evidence base with mechanically verified
  citations, a Lakatosian statement of the programme's hard core and its
  killers, an adversarial multi-model harness in which refutation is the
  default verdict, and a public ledger of refuted conjectures. Contains no
  patient data and produces no medical advice.
keywords:
  - neuropathic pain
  - nociception
  - neuromodulation
  - dorsal root ganglion
  - research programme
  - adversarial evaluation
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
license-url: "https://github.com/davidvanheeswijck/pain-as-information/blob/main/LICENSE"
